  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5402",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is linked to GMS-10 through a series of molecular interactions involving purinoceptors and other compounds. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin acts as a target for P2X purinoceptor 1, which is in turn targeted by palmarumycin CP18, and this pathway leads to GMS-10. Similarly, doxorubicin is also linked to NCI-H1522, which is targeted by palmarumycin CP18, and this same compound targets GMS-10. Additionally, doxorubicin is associated with Mollicellin N, which also targets GMS-10. These findings collectively indicate that doxorubicin may exert its effects through a shared mechanism involving palmarumycin CP18, which acts as a bridge between doxorubicin and GMS-10. The consistent presence of palmarumycin CP18 in these relationships suggests a potential role in mediating the interaction between doxorubicin and GMS-10, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
